title Fold R -- weigh_the_term, and the absentee a single accessor brought home
prompt Kyri voice and Radiant Style first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries, Standfast on reds, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota one doc, sweep the prose Radiant, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. crux/REDS.md reads clean -- REDS %110 was booked and closed on 20260821.073606, its repair a property rather than a rule, and no agent-closable red stands open. The line is free for constructive work.
think The running thread is unambiguous. The three newest logs are folds O, P, and Q of the Caravan ladder arc, and fold Q's recommend names weigh_the_term the better crux of the queue's top three -- thirty rungs against provision_notes' twenty-four, and a body less likely to reach a rung's own wire.
think Rota lap 1472 mod 27 = 14 -- context/RADIANT_STYLE.md with context/TWILIGHT_STYLE.md. Both read whole this lap, which the voice-first instruction had already begun. The pass playbook's bound is the one that governed this round's prose: style only, claims held exactly.
think Fold O's lesson runs first, every lap: a fold queue is a lead rather than a verdict. So every body named weigh_the_term was hashed before a line moved. The queue said thirty; the ladder holds thirty-one. The thirty-first, lapse.rye, differs in six places -- and reading the diff, all six are one difference.
think lapse.rye owns the lapsing tier. It reaches report_out.unbounded directly where the thirty rungs above reach lapsing_of(report_out).unbounded. That is precisely fold M's shape on recant.rye and fold J's on the staircase, which means the answer was already written twice: a rung that owns a tier can name the reach anyway, and three lines of identity accessor fold sixty-nine.
think So absentees come in two kinds, and this is the finding worth keeping. Fold Q found five dated OUT of their family by a shape born after them -- those stay home named, since folding them would add behavior. This lap found one that was never dated out at all, only unnamed, and an accessor brought it home. The reading to make about an absentee is which kind stands before you.
think Surveying the sixteen symbols the body names found fourteen already public in all thirty-one rungs, plus four types and a bound. Only lapsing_of needed widening, in twenty-two rungs. Fold P's lesson again -- a fold pays its successors, and the honest price of a fold is charged once and spent several times.
think Before widening, the split question fold Q taught: a declaration line belongs to the body it opens, so making a symbol public in some holders and not others cuts a family in two. Hashed all thirty lapsing_of bodies -- thirty distinct texts, since each names its own rung's report type. Thirty singletons carry zero, so the widening splits nothing and hands back nothing. Free for the simpler of the two reasons fold Q named.
obs The queue's own number was wrong by one in the direction that matters. It printed thirty rungs, and the thirty-first was not a stranger to the family -- it was the rung that OWNS the tier the other thirty reach into. A meter that keys bodies by exact text can never see that, because the difference it reads as distinctness is the very fact of ownership. Reading past the queue found it for the second lap running, and the scan's header now carries both kinds of absentee so the next lap reads for the difference rather than for one shape.
obs Both arithmetics close with no remainder, and each was measured rather than assumed. In carry: the family gave back 2,001 -- twenty-nine copies of sixty-nine, since lapse.rye stood unique and carried nothing at all -- the three-line delegates carry 90 across thirty copies, and 2,001 less 90 is the 1,911 the meter measured. On disk: thirty rungs shed sixty-six lines apiece, lapse.rye shed sixty-six and gained thirteen for its accessor, the harness took a hundred and three, and 1,930 is the fall wc reports over the tracked rungs.
obs A 168-line gap opened between the raw glob and the tracked count, and it resolved cleanly rather than mysteriously: caravan/parse_int.rye and caravan/tally_copy.rye are untracked symlinks that HEAD does not hold. Reporting the fall over tracked rungs keeps the number comparable to every fold before it, and naming why is what keeps a discrepancy from becoming a drift.
loom fold=weigh_the_term rungs=31 body_lines=69 widenings=22 carry_before=129478 carry_after=127567 carry_fall=1911 disk_fall=1930 delegates_carry=90 choir_witnesses=105
